{"term":"produce","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:11f27e5737eb3aa0d8","definition":"To bring forth, to yield, make, manufacture, or otherwise generate.","example":"[chapter XIII, page 264:] […] the greatest jurist that his country had produced. […] [chapter XVI, page 644:] At Rome the news from Ireland produced a sensation of a very different kind.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["make","generate","yield","create","bring forth","cause","contrive","create","ferment","forge","develop","engender","evolve","generate","gin up","innate","form","forthbring","make","produce","spawn"],"antonyms":["destroy","ruin"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coproduce","executive produce","exec-produce","handproduce","hyperproduce","interproduce","mass-produce","misproduce","outproduce","overproduce","preproduce","producement","reproduce","underproduce"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/produce#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:32830c776c36c3be0d","definition":"To make or yield something.","example":"Now it is also my understanding, I believe I am correct in this, that either one or two other manufacturers did not produce this year, which also created a certain shortage.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["coproduce","executive produce","exec-produce","handproduce","hyperproduce","interproduce","mass-produce","misproduce","outproduce","overproduce","preproduce","producement","reproduce","underproduce"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/produce#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a904fd66d8dee21d8b","definition":"To make (a thing) available to a person, an authority, etc.; to provide for inspection.","example":"It was necessary for the prisoner to produce a witness to prove his innocency.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["present","offer"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coproduce","executive produce","exec-produce","handproduce","hyperproduce","interproduce","mass-produce","misproduce","outproduce","overproduce","preproduce","producement","reproduce","underproduce"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/produce#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cabf574aac6b861810","definition":"To sponsor and present (a motion picture, etc) to an audience or to the public.","example":"David Tickle flew in to Melbourne to produce the quad-platinum (in Australia) LP “True Colors” and the triple gold single “I Got You”— both of which shot the band to international prominence.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coproduce","executive produce","exec-produce","handproduce","hyperproduce","interproduce","mass-produce","misproduce","outproduce","overproduce","preproduce","producement","reproduce","underproduce"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/produce#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d256d8e4247a3afb52","definition":"To extend an area, or lengthen a line.","example":"to produce a side of a triangle","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coproduce","executive produce","exec-produce","handproduce","hyperproduce","interproduce","mass-produce","misproduce","outproduce","overproduce","preproduce","producement","reproduce","underproduce"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/produce#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8f5f2c7c14acc33b28","definition":"To draw out; to extend; to lengthen or prolong.","example":"And truely there goes a great deale of providence to produce a mans life unto threeſcore; […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["coproduce","executive produce","exec-produce","handproduce","hyperproduce","interproduce","mass-produce","misproduce","outproduce","overproduce","preproduce","producement","reproduce","underproduce"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/produce#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5a17e452b9f8931d88","definition":"To alter using technology, as opposed to simply performing.","example":"highly produced sound","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["coproduce","executive produce","exec-produce","handproduce","hyperproduce","interproduce","mass-produce","misproduce","outproduce","overproduce","preproduce","producement","reproduce","underproduce"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/produce#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4c06e919537331f428","definition":"That which is produced.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["output","proceeds","product","yield"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["coproduce","executive produce","exec-produce","handproduce","hyperproduce","interproduce","mass-produce","misproduce","outproduce","overproduce","preproduce","producement","reproduce","underproduce","bioproduce","produce broker","produce race"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/produce#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:782eabca13ecd1d9a9","definition":"Harves